\import{base-macros}

\p{\strong{Status:} accepted and carried out. The machine is the default engine. It was the default for 54 minutes in the afternoon of 2026-11-24, was withdrawn, and was made the default again on 2026-11-25 at 03:05 UTC, which is 22:05 local time on 2026-11-24, when the condition of step 3 was met; see step 4 and [the changelog entry](log-65Z0). This note was written between the two; the paragraph on the state of the condition is of that time, and step 4 and the evidence for it were added on 2026-11-24 after the second change. A note of 2026-11-25 follows the evidence of step 4: one condition under which that evidence was taken, the re-check of every rejection, no longer holds for a plain run.}

\p{\strong{Context.} A run that names no engine uses the non-reference engine with the highest priority of at least 100, and the [reference engine](design-reference-engine) if there is none. The machine's priority is one line, \code{\verb~|MachineProvider.priority()~}: 100 makes it the default, 10 does not. Nothing else in the launcher changes with it. As primary engine the machine has every rejection re-checked and every decline decided by the reference engine, see [the verdict protocol](design-verdict-protocol). That was the protocol when this was decided and until 2026-11-25; since then a rejection of the machine is final in a plain run and only the declines go to the reference engine, see the note below.}

\p{\strong{Decision, in four steps.}}

\ol{
\li{\strong{Made at 19:41Z.} The integrator of wave 6 set the priority to 100 together with the new [default switch set](dec-LZFX), on the gates listed below.}
\li{\strong{Withdrawn at 20:35Z.} The orchestrator set the priority back to 10. The agent working on eager reduction had written 67 hostile exports with official verdicts, and they showed a family of wrong accepts against the official checker, findings E1-F1 to E1-F5. A bound variable was typed by what its environment slot holds (the value of a let, the argument of a re-inferred beta redex, the comparison variable of the other side), or an expected type was kept as a lambda's own. Such a type is only convertible with the declared one, and the official comparison is not transitive. Three of the five were in the generic tier v0, two in the switch \code{expect}.}
\li{\strong{The condition for making it again.} As first written: the five findings are fixed, the new exports are strict rows of the hostile suite, and the gates have been run again. As refined later the same evening by the maintainer's choice of [practical exactness](dec-TQSI): the machine may be the default engine once the gates show items (a) to (c) of the [exactness contract](design-exactness-contract) and an adversarial review of the candidate has found no kind F.}
\li{\strong{Made again at 03:05 UTC on 2026-11-25.} The integrator of the machine set the priority to 100 as a publication of its own, ten minutes after [the default switch set](dec-YP0N) had been published, with the evidence below stated before the change and checked again after it. A run that means the reference engine now says \code{\verb~|-X engine=reference~} or \code{\verb~|-X policy=strict~}.}
}

\p{\strong{Evidence at the time it was made.} All of it on the main tree as published at 19:10Z, machine jar \code{78c74ca92785}:}

\table{
\tr{\th{Gate}\th{Result}}
\tr{\td{Hostile suite, in process}\td{32 switch sets by 329 exports, 10,528 judgments against the official verdict: 0 unexpected, no known finding still reproduces.}}
\tr{\td{The machine's gate, v0 and the default set}\td{Pass with declines. SOUNDNESS 0 and COMPLETENESS 0 on all 230 arena tests (15,845 engine checks), Init, Std, reachability and the Cedar slice; tier equivalence, convention equivalence and audits with 0 differences. Every decline of the default set is eager reduction.}}
\tr{\td{Mutants through the real driver, v0 and the default set}\td{17,775 mutants per set: SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0; 1,008,568 declarations per set with no disagreement in either direction.}}
\tr{\td{Differential engine through the JVM launcher, default configuration}\td{0 differences on 760,839 units: the 230 tests, the Cedar slice, reachability, Init, Std, con-leche, cedar and cslib. Every unit not compared is an eager-reduction decline of the machine. The commit message that recorded the step gives 760,113 units.}}
\tr{\td{The corpora with the machine as primary engine, 8 workers, native image}\td{All accepted, nothing rejected by the machine, declines for eager reduction only, for example 6,711 of 714,712 engine checks on Mathlib.}}
}

\p{\strong{Why none of the evidence of the first time saw the findings.} Every gate compared the machine with the reference engine, on real corpora and on mutants, where the declared type and the convertible one are the same type; and the 329 hostile exports had been written before this shape was known and had no such row. In the integrator's words, 0 differences on 760,839 units said nothing about verdicts that need a declared type to differ from a convertible one; a review with new hostile exports belongs before a change of the default engine, not after it.}

\p{\strong{State of the condition when this was written.} The fix of E1-F1 to E1-F6 is published (typed bindings: a bound variable carries its declared type; machine jar \code{5945b6568177}), and 92 rows of this family are in the hostile suite, 6 of them marked kind T. On that jar the full gate for v0 and the default set shows no wrong verdict and no difference, the mutants are at 0 and 0 for both sets, and the differential engine shows 0 verdict differences on 1,153,493 engine checks. The adversarial review of the default set and of the candidate default found no kind F on 987 hostile rows; what it found is kind T and is recorded in [the divergence classes](design-official-divergence), among them E1-F7, which the machine still accepts. The priority in the tree was nevertheless still 10: a new integration of the machine had been started and had not reported. Step 4 is what it reported.}

\p{\strong{Evidence at the time it was made again.} All of it on the code that was published or on the published jar; the machine jar with the priority is byte for byte the jar of the distribution that passed the gate of the first row.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Gate}\th{Result}}
\tr{\td{The gate of a default configuration on a machine-default distribution, no option anywhere, every step judged by official verdicts}\td{230 of 230 published tests correct, none declined. 17,775 mutants: SOUNDNESS 0 and COMPLETENESS 0, 15,741 in agreement and 2,034 declined. The differential self-test caught. The hostile suite, 1,196 rows: 1,124 in agreement, 68 tolerated accepts of kind T, 4 declined, no wrong accept and no wrong reject.}}
\tr{\td{The adversarial pass with official verdicts on this switch set}\td{No kind F. Its conditions are met: named switches that bring \code{facts} and \code{probes}, its 423 rows in the suite with their kinds, finding S3-F7 fixed, the strict re-check still deciding every rejection of the machine.}}
\tr{\td{Differential engine through that launcher}\td{1,141,195 checks on the 230 tests, Init, Std, cedar, cslib and 16 Mathlib slices: 0 differences. With the same switch set given by name, on the distribution of the timing table: con-leche 36,272 of 36,274 units compared, navier-stokes-euler 124,834 of 124,850, reachability 4,224.}}
\tr{\td{The eight corpora}\td{All accepted: on the JVM launcher of the machine-default distribution with no option, 8 and 4 workers; on the native image with the machine named as engine, 8 and 4 workers.}}
\tr{\td{The machine's gate and the mutants}\td{Full gate of the default set on the frozen final tree and again on the main tree before the publication: pass with declines, SOUNDNESS 0 and COMPLETENESS 0 (all 230 tests 15,804 accepted, 41 rejected, none declined; Init 57,938; Std 100,095 and 1 declined; reachability 4,224; the Cedar slice 8,064). The slow hostile matrix, 56 switch sets by 1,196 rows. Mutants for v0 and the default set, 17,775 each: SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0.}}
\tr{\td{The arena's build-and-run test on the machine-default main tree}\td{Run right after the publication, because it builds from the main tree and could not see the change before; announced beforehand as the one deviation, with the priority to be taken back at once on a failure. It passed.}}
\tr{\td{The gate again on the distribution the team shares, built from the frozen set of jars}\td{Through the executable and through the jars: the counts of the first row.}}
}

\p{\strong{Note of 2026-11-25: the re-check is no longer part of a plain run.} The adversarial pass of the second row was made with "the strict re-check still deciding every rejection of the machine", and the first row counted "no wrong reject" on the hostile suite with that re-check in force. Since the change of 2026-11-25 (\commit{a8dc6dd}) a rejection of the machine is final by default, by the maintainer's instruction that the reference engine is not to affect production; see [the decision](dec-PUU0). The machine stays the default engine. What the evidence above established for item (a), no accept of a statement that is not derivable, carries over: turning the re-check off can only turn an accept into a rejection or a decline. What no longer holds for a plain run is "no wrong reject" on hand-made files: 12 rows of the hostile suite that the official checker accepts are now rejected, the rows that the re-check used to repair, see [accepted risks](accepted-risks-wrong-rejects). On the eight corpora, the arena tests and the mutants no verdict got worse. The configuration under which the evidence of this note was taken is still there by name, \code{\verb~|-X verify=reference~}, and its gate gives the counts of the build before the change: no wrong reject, 15,741 mutants in agreement and 2,034 declined, and on the hostile suite, which has 1,274 rows since 2026-11-25, 1,192 in agreement, 78 tolerated accepts and 4 declined; see [the census](rep-MO-1), section 8.}

\p{\strong{What was different the second time.} The first change rested on gates that compare the machine with the reference engine. The second rested on official verdicts: an adversarial pass with new hostile exports before the change, as [the rule](dec-QN1O) asks; a hostile suite in which every row has the official verdict and a kind; and a gate of the distribution as a user runs it. Two findings that came up while it was prepared were closed first, [a stale entry of the level store](log-XNVE) and [a rejection of official accepts through dropped metadata](log-TRJ0).}

\p{\strong{Consequences.}}

\ul{
\li{After the withdrawal the default switch set, the session cap and the measurements of wave 6 stood for \code{\verb~|-X engine=machine~}, and the benchmark tables name the engine of every row. Since step 4 a plain run is the machine with [the default set of that evening](dec-YP0N), and the tables are [regenerated for it](rep-benchmarks).}
\li{The hostile suite gained the rows of this family, a kind column, and a step in the end-to-end guard that judges every row by its official verdict; see [the gate](design-gate).}
\li{A change of the default engine or of a default set now needs an adversarial pass first, see [the rule](dec-QN1O).}
\li{The addendum to the first soundness review, on which the change had rested, carries the remark that it should not have been read as a review: its list of what was not reviewed was the warning.}
}

\p{Detail: [the switch reference](design-switches-document) (the note at its top and the table of gates), [the integration notes of the machine](rep-machine-INT) section 3, [the soundness review of the machine](rep-soundness-machine) section 7, [the working notes of package M5](rep-machine-M5) (the fix), [the record of the divergence classes](rep-official-divergence) section 6. Source: [the wave-6 session](ses-CVTE), [the exactness session](ses-874D) and, for step 4, [the finalization session](ses-A14B).}

\p{Findings, examples and open problems: [a gate that compares with the reference engine cannot see a divergence both engines share](ins-SJW4), [the problem of making the machine the default engine](prob-W2FV), closed by step 4, and [what the release leaves open](prob-HC9J).}
